From a4972911afd113b381c52371abd907d445c32fd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ake Rehnman <ake.rehnman@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:41:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu: invalidate display state when resetting scanouts

Resetting virtio-vga returns display updates to VGA, but leaves its cached
mode unchanged even though the virtio scanout may have replaced the
console surface.

If the guest resumes the same VGA mode, VGA can reuse an incompatible
surface. This can leave the display black or cause an out-of-bounds write
when the VGA mode is larger than the surface.

Invalidate each scanout's console after clearing the virtio state. With
g->enable cleared, virtio-vga forwards the invalidation to VGA, forcing
it to recreate the surface on the next display update.
---
 hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c
index 270fbaae102..3eef0f3f0c7 100644
--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c
@@ -35,6 +35,12 @@ virtio_gpu_base_reset(VirtIOGPUBase *g)
         g->scanout[i].x = 0;
         g->scanout[i].y = 0;
         g->scanout[i].ds = NULL;
+
+        /*
+         * virtio-vga now uses VGA again. Its mode can be unchanged while
+         * the virtio scanout has replaced the console's display surface.
+         */
+        qemu_console_hw_invalidate(g->scanout[i].con);
     }
 }
 
